# Copy to .env for local work. Nothing here is committed.
#
# Two kinds of value live in this file and they go in DIFFERENT places on
# Cloudflare Pages:
#
#   BUILD-TIME — read by Astro while the site is compiled and baked into the
#                HTML. Anything here is public once the site ships.
#
#   RUNTIME    — read by functions/api/brief.ts on each request. These never
#                reach the browser and must not be moved into the build scope.
#
# CLOUDFLARE-SETUP.md §4 says exactly which box each one goes in.


# ---- RUNTIME (secret) ----------------------------------------------------

# Formspree form id — the part after /f/ in the endpoint URL.
# Read by the brief function and forwarded server-side. It used to be a build
# variable, which put the endpoint into the HTML of all 45 pages; it is now
# server-side only. The old value is in the git history of the legacy
# index.html, so treat it as known and rotate it if that matters.
FORMSPREE_ID=xxxxxxxx

# Cloudflare Turnstile SECRET key, paired with the site key below.
# Used only for the siteverify call. With this unset the function skips
# verification, which is what keeps local builds and previews usable — so be
# sure it IS set in production.
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=


# ---- BUILD-TIME (public) -------------------------------------------------

# Cloudflare Turnstile SITE key. Public by design; it identifies the widget in
# the page. With no key the widget is not rendered and the Turnstile script is
# never loaded.
TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# Self-hosted Umami. BOTH must be set for anything to be emitted; with either
# missing no script tag is produced and no request is made — a half-configured
# tracker is worse than none.
#
# The ORIGIN of UMAMI_SCRIPT_URL is also what the generated Content-Security-
# Policy allows in script-src and connect-src, so moving the instance updates
# the CSP on the next build. Editing dist/_headers by hand will not survive.
UMAMI_SCRIPT_URL=
UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID=
